prompt Keaton said kg linengrow, after I asked to check the number first.
think Ran the check with the CURRENT pattern this time rather than the one that had shared the meter's bug. No comment above, no trailing comment, no alternative spelling. 41.6% is real, and linengrow is the first room in eight where the number held.
think Then asked whether a class-based sweep would be honest. Grouped all 242 uncovered asserts by shape: the largest family is 10, and the tail is long. No shortcut survives that, so the files were read.
obs Swept the eight densest: tube_manifest 16, seva_jabs2_glass_audience 16, dexter_glass_keyboard_paint 28, dexter_glass_emoji 12, hearth_lulu1 24, tube2_publish 10, glow_seva_b0_replay 7, glow_seva_b0_append 7 -- 57 blocks in all.
obs The reasons that mattered most were the layout ones. hearth_lulu1 divides a window into cells, and a zero in any of window_w, window_h or grid_rows divides by zero rather than laying out a grid -- three asserts, one reason, and nothing had said it.
obs seva_jabs2_glass_audience carries a comptime assert that keyboard_row0 equals skate_row0 plus audience_rows. That is one layout arithmetic checked where it is written rather than two constants free to drift apart, and it deserved to say so.
obs dexter_glass_emoji proves its atlas at compile time -- forty faces, real codepoints, distinct glyphs. A duplicate glyph would paint two keys the same and give a finger no way to tell them apart, which is what the assert is actually for.
obs glow_seva_b0_replay compares two replays of one log and asserts their roots agree. That is the whole promise a replay makes, and the line now says so instead of restating the comparison.
obs linengrow 41.6% to 62.6%, gap 239 to 153. Tree 95%, gap 767. The remaining 153 sit across 56 small files at two or three each.
